  "description": "Cross-Scale MAE is a self-supervised masked autoencoder model for remote sensing, designed to learn robust multi-scale representations by enforcing cross-scale consistency at both structural and semantic levels using contrastive and generative losses. It leverages scale augmentation and xFormers for efficient training.",
